DESCRIPTION:National Gunpowder Day falls on November 5\, the anniversary of
  the night in 1605 when a man was found in a cellar beneath the Palace of 
 Westminster with 36 barrels of gunpowder and a plan to kill the king and m
 ost of England's government. Who created the observance\, and whether the 
 date was chosen for that reason\, is not documented in any reliable source
 . The plot itself is documented exhaustively\, and it is the reason Novemb
 er 5 means anything at all.\n\nhttps://todaycelebrates.com/holiday/nationa
 l-gunpowder-day/
